# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Blind_spot_spb / v11 — what does NOT go in the repo.
#
# Rule: analysis-grade artifacts (jsonl/json/csv panels, ~53 MB) are COMMITTED,
# because `make freeze` must be reproducible from a clone. Weight-grade dumps
# (~9.5 GB of trained contrast vectors) are NOT: they are regenerable by GPU
# from the committed corpora + configs, and no number in the paper reads them
# directly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- weight-grade dumps: regenerable, huge ---
# The support dumps live in <panel>/supports/*.npz. Naming only the panel dirs
# missed them and staged 431 MB of tensors; scripts/pack_artifacts.sh had the
# identical omission. Both now name the directory AND the extension.
results/directions/
results/directions_r128/
results/sketches/
results/sketches_expE/
results/profiles/
results/profiles_base/
**/supports/
checkpoints/
*.npz
*.npy
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt

# --- shipped result bundles (superseded by the committed panels) ---
*.zip

# --- editor / interpreter noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# --- timestamped backups: the repo IS the history now ---
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.orig

# --- run-local scratch ---
results/scratch/
logs/*.log
!logs/.gitkeep
work/
*.tmp

# --- secrets: never ---
.env
.env.*
*_token
hf_token*

# --- third-party checkouts: cloned, not vendored ---
# Each carries its own .git, so committing them would either nest a foreign
# history or create a gitlink nothing can resolve. external/README.md records
# the exact commits instead.
external/*
!external/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY. This is a CODE repo.
#
# The panels (~43 MB) and elicited corpora (~11 MB) were 93% of the tree by
# size and are not source. They ship the way this project has always shipped
# results -- as an archive, via scripts/pack_artifacts.sh -- and are restored
# into results/ on whichever box is doing analysis. See DATA.md.
#
# Kept in git despite living under these trees: nothing. `make freeze` needs
# them restored first; `bash run.sh` does not (run_unit.py re-elicits any
# corpus it is missing).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/
results_v9/

# A stray v1-era panel dump that sat at the repo root, outside results/,
# and so slipped past the rule above.
/removal.jsonl

# Rendered figures are build outputs of `make figures`; the audited
# fig*_data.csv they are drawn from ARE tracked.
figures/*.pdf
figures/*.png
